Undoubtedly, and if that had not been so, the hon. gentleman will credit us with such a degree of intelligence that we would not have built those railways if it had not been for the development of the ^vhole country. If it had been useless for Canada to develop the Western Provinces, those railways would not have been built;
they were bdilt for the development 11 p.m. of the Western Provinces. Those railways have in a very large measure paid the bill; they have given to the Western Provinces a greatly increased value. Who has been bene^ted by the increased

value given to the Western Provinces by the construction of railways, if not first and above all, the westerner himself?
